 {"question" "q-127397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(-2,3,3)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨2,-5,3⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-2)}{2}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z-3}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{2}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z-3}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+2}{-2}=\\frac{y-3}{5}=\\frac{z+3}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+2}{2}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z-3}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-2}{-2}=\\frac{y+5}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+3}{-5}=\\frac{z-3}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+5}{-3}=\\frac{z-3}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+2}{2}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z-3}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line with the vector equation\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(7,-2,4)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y-(-2)}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-127406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+1}{7}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-3}{-4}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+7}{1}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-1}{7}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{3}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{-2}=\\frac{z-0}{1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z,\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+3}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-3:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5-2t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+3}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z,\\,x=-3\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-71045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x}{-3}=\\frac{y+2}{5},\\,z=1"] ["math" "\\frac{y+5}{-2}=z,\\,x=3"] ["math" "\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z,\\,x=-3"] ["math" "x+3=\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z"] ["math" "x+3=z,\\,y=5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z,\\,x=-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-1}{-2}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=2:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3+3t \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1-2t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ part and instead write $y=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\\,y=2\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-127412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+3}{-3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},\\,y=2"] ["math" "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{z+1}{-2},\\,y=-2"] ["math" "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\\,y=2"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{z+1}{-2},\\,y=2"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\\,y=-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\\,y=2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y-(-9)}{2}=\\frac{z-11}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2}=\\frac{z-11}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{z-11}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=11:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7-3t \\\\ -9+2t \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-11}{0}$ part and instead write $z=11$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2},\\,z=11\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-71039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{y-2}{-9},\\,z=0"] ["math" "\\frac{x+7}{-3}=\\frac{y-9}{2},\\,z=-11"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2},\\,z=11"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2}=z-11"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=z-11,\\,y=-9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2},\\,z=11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{-3}=\\frac{z-6}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3}=\\frac{z-6}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{z-6}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=6:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3+7t \\\\ -1-3t \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-6}{0}$ part and instead write $z=6$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3},\\,z=6\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-71048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{y-1}{-3},\\,z=-6"] ["math" "\\frac{x+7}{3}=\\frac{y-3}{-1},\\,z=0"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3},\\,z=6"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3}=z-6"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{3}=\\frac{y+3}{-1},\\,z=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-71048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3},\\,z=6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{7}=\\frac{y-5}{0}=\\frac{z}{2}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{y-5}{0}=\\frac{z}{2},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{y-5}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=5:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3+7t \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y-5}{0}$ part and instead write $y=5$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-127454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+3}{2}=\\frac{z}{7},\\,y=5"] ["math" "\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{z-2}{1},\\,y=5"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{z-2}{2},\\,y=5"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(3,-5,7)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨3,6,9⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y-(-5)}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-33249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{y+6}{-5}=\\frac{z+9}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{y-5}{6}=\\frac{z+7}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y-6}{-5}=\\frac{z-9}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{y}{6}=\\frac{z}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/1f9599192c1979f40fc519458019ed3296d9a5ef9048aaed41aab973c62e0be8.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-2,3,1)$ and $Q(5,-1,4).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,4⟩-⟨-2,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-2)}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-1}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-1}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-33234" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33234" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+2}{2}=\\frac{y-3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{1}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+2}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+7}{2}=\\frac{y+4}{3},\\,z=3"] ["math" "\\frac{x+7}{2}=\\frac{y+4}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{1}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{7}=\\frac{y}{-4}=\\frac{z}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-33234" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+2}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/44b0b683358bb448229380402717f396d13f82d2904bbf1ece1fcf9fd4567f14.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that the line passes through the points $P(7,-2,4)$ and $Q(1,1,4).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,4⟩-⟨7,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y-(-2)}{3}=\\frac{z-4}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3}=\\frac{z-4}{0}.\n$$\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because $\\frac{z-4}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=4.$ For example, our two points $P(7,-2,4)$ and $Q(1,1,4)$ both have $z$-coordinates of $z=4.$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-4}{0}$ part and instead write $z=4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3},\\,z=4\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-127535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{-3},\\,z=4"] ["math" "\\frac{x+7}{-6}=\\frac{y-2}{-3},\\,z=-4"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3},\\,z=4"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{6}=\\frac{y-2}{3},\\,z=-4"] ["math" "\\frac{x-7}{6}=\\frac{y-2}{3},\\,z=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-127535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3},\\,z=4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-32827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(0,-1,3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-32827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-0}{2}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{-1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "570dda02acd57c60b6e215edeae92ca8ed4b949c6322d76e5af575968de3ade1"} {"question" "q-32827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e"} {"question" "q-32827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answe